The claim is mechanically pinned: after normalizing only explicit empty-list constructors (`.Exprs`, `.ParamNames`, `.Stmts`) back to surface syntax, `kast` produces byte-identical constructor trees for the regenerated `solution.mpy` and the program inside `SPEC.sort-array`. All three preconditions also have concrete witnesses, and a ground substitution claim closes.

The important limitation is now clear: the whole-program claim closes by itself, without either key claim, because symbolic `sorted` returns the fixed semantics’ opaque `sortVS`/`sortKeyVS` terms. That is an explicit supplied-primitive trust boundary, not a proof-local shortcut, but the bridge from those terms to “stable sorting by popcount” remains conditional and will affect the final status.
Fresh builds and all positive claims succeeded. Constructor-level KAST comparison pins the entry claim to the regenerated program; ground witnesses satisfy every precondition. Static review identified the supplied sort primitives as the sole material opaque result boundary.
